  "reason": "invoice_export unblocked: a name wrapping at a hyphen rejoined as LONG- SLEEVE and read as a missing field, which had been failing every recapture; also n5 -> n6, which had been drawing 5 of 6 thermal layouts since notebook_ledger",
  "replaced": "Recapture, two reasons at once: (1) items_table()/_header_rows()/_group_row()/_item_row()/_item_extras() in sheets/base.py now build a components.table.TableSpec instead of hand-rolled <tr>/<td> strings -- column widths move from a width: style on each header <th> to <colgroup><col style=width:...%>, which is not guaranteed byte-identical under table-layout:auto even though every family's own CSS still draws the actual borders/shading/zebra unchanged (border=Border.none(), cls= passthrough); (2) this baseline was already stale independent of that work -- last captured at a8ea2f4, before 9d2c97d and other rulebase/rules, rulebase/corpus changes that never got a recapture (metadata schema was None, now 8), and before the layout count grew from 14 to 16 (tools/baseline.py's own plan names, n14 -> n16). Both kinds of drift are folded into this one capture since a plan's images say nothing about either until it is retaken."
